    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41471" root="هيت" body-key="h">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هيّت بِهِ</span></b> , (S, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهْيِيتٌ</span>, (TA,) as
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هوّت</span>, (S,) <i>He cried out to him, and called</i>

<i>him,</i> (S, K,) <i>saying,</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَيْتَ هَيْتَ</span>; or saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَاهْ يَاهْ</span>,
which is a cry by which a pastor calls his companion from afar; or, accord. to AZ, saying
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَا هَيَا</span> [or rather <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَاهَيَاهْ</span>: see art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يه</span>]. (TA.)

